    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0656" n="642" xml:id="pg642"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.009/7–150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-01T13:00:00+01:00">July 1, 1950—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Embtel 3733 June 29 repeated Paris, The Hague and Brussels.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d393-f1"/> It was suggested to Tomlinson Foreign Office, this
                    morning that in view favorable response France, Belgium and Netherlands there
                    appeared to be no obstacles to immediate application export controls to China
                    and North Korea.</p>
                <p>Tomlinson, after consultation by telephone with British missions concerned, has
                    arranged for Colonial Office to ask Hong Kong and Singapore apply controls
                    immediately. Controls already in force in UK.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 5; repeated info Paris 2, The Hague 1, Brussels 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d393-f1" n="1" xml:id="d393-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. It reported that Mr. Tomlinson of the Foreign Office had transmitted
                    to the other British Government offices concerned a paper recommending that the
                    United States position on application of export controls to China and North
                    Korea be supported by the United Kingdom immediately (493.009/6–2950).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
